        "id": "fd_0382",
        "title": "Proof-Complexity Holography via Persistent Resolution Homology",
        "description": "Conjecture: For every unsatisfiable CNF formula F, there exists a canonically defined filtered simplicial complex K(F) built from clause interactions along bounded-width resolution such that the total persistence of H_1(K(F)) is polynomially equivalent to minimum clause space up to universal constants on standard families (pebbling, Tseitin, random k-CNF near threshold). Test: Explicitly define K(F), compute its persistence on benchmark CNF families, and check whether formulas with provably high clause space also exhibit proportionally large 1-dimensional persistence, while low-space formulas do not. A single infinite family with asymptotically separated behavior refutes the conjecture. Impact: This would create a new topological invariant for proof complexity, potentially turning lower-bound questions into computable TDA problems and enabling structure-aware SAT heuristics based on persistent homology signatures.",
